# The Prolog backend's encodings, chosen by positive candidacy of one layer
# of hindley_milner_unions' structures. A knowledge module of one backend, enabled with the type check when
# the Prolog backend is: the backend represents natively the members of
# nat_type, as big integers, and of boolean_type (prolog_backend.pl).
#
# A type is a CANDIDATE for a representation when its class holds
# `candidate r` of it, r the filter whose members the representation holds.
# A structure of two alternatives whose second has exactly one field is a
# candidate for the naturals, whatever its first alternative, and its field
# is one too: it is unified with its candidacy, and hindley_milner_unions'
# unification unites them. A structure of two alternatives whose second has
# no field is a candidate for the booleans. The layer read is the one that
# tells the backend's representations apart (one field, no field), and a
# cycle of any length through such layers, an infinite datum's type
# included, is a candidate, read with no closed-world step: every lemma
# here only adds, so that adding knowledge adds candidates and typed
# versions and takes none away (CONTRIBUTING.md, "Soundness, monotonicity,
# modularity, budgets": monotonicity in knowledge).
#
# A function type whose domain (and range) is a candidate gets a MARKER in
# its class, one node by congruence for each representation however many
# function types the class holds, so that a name's occurrences, which share
# one class of types, meet each marker once and the typed versions stay
# linear. The typed versions and the contracts are written where a marker
# is, by lemmas whose left side requires it: a typed version f (x ∥ r)
# where the domain is a candidate for r, and (f (x ∥ r)) ∥ s where the range
# is one for s too; a contract λy. f y + (f (y ∥ r)) ∥ s where both are. A
# class that is a candidate for two representations, in a program HM
# rejects, gets the typed versions of both, and the extraction picks among
# them by its ranks.
#
# The representation is an argument of the candidacy and of the markers, so
# that only the shapes and the naturals' field are lemmas of one
# representation, and every other lemma is one for every representation:
# a fixed number of lemmas rules out lemmas for each type.
#
# Every equation of the zero universe has both sides top up to contextual
# equivalence;
# each typed version and contract is sound for every filter, as
# hindley_milner_unions' were (the paper proofs their declarations cite).
#
# A class can be a candidate for a representation its values are not: a
# candidacy pushed into a field from an enclosing structure, the naturals'
# field or a list cell's head and tail, as in a Maybe whose payload is no
# natural; or a program's own data that coincide with the library's in the
# layer a candidacy reads, a hand-written Either whose right has successor's
# body while its left has a field. Where the class's own type refutes the
# candidacy (the refutation lemmas below), each filter of a typed version by
# r over the class is under the repeller $repelled, so that the extraction
# keeps the untyped version at that call and the typed one wherever the
# candidacy holds. A refuted candidacy says that the values have no native
# representation of r, not that the program has no type: under recursive
# types such a program has one, and missing a native representation only
# slows a program down. A typed version that stays filters its values by
# r, and each one's fallback point reads the value's heads once and takes
# the untyped path, decoding nothing (lambda_jit_jit, A FALLBACK POINT;
# measured 2026-10-29); a dispatch strategy that rejects throws on such a
# value (lambda_jit_baseline_dispatch_strategies).
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "hindley_milner_unions") "shapes")
λ structure alternative no_alternative field no_field _
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "prolog_backend_shapes") "prolog_backend_shapes")
λ candidate contract_at domain_candidate function_candidate item_candidate list_item_candidate refuted
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "native_types") "natural")
λ _ _ _ nat_type
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "native_types") "boolean")
λ _ _ boolean_type _
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "hindley_milner_unions") "judgments")
λ _ _ unify
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "native_types") "list")
λ _ _ _ list_type
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "hindley_milner_unions") "types")
λ function_type _ _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "native_types") "markers")
λ _ _ _ _ $repelled
