    λ _ lemmas _
    . lemmas
      # ---- the contracts of curried functions ----
      #
      # A function whose type's domain is a candidate for r and whose range g is a
      # function type of a candidate domain is the closure λy. f y + k (f (y ∥ r)),
      # k the range's contract contract_at g; contract_at g is λf. f for every g,
      # so the closure's body is f y + f (y ∥ r), which is f y since
      # f y ⊑ f (y ∥ r), and λy. f y is f by the η rule. contract_at of a
      # function type is, one layer of the type for each instance, the closure
      # that takes f and filters its argument by the domain's representation and
      # its result by the range's: by the range's own contract at a function type
      # of a candidate domain, by the range's filter at a candidate. The arity of
      # a curried function is walked on its type, an object term, with no lemma
      # for each arity.
      #
      # The closure is written as the redex (λk. λy. …) (contract_at g), which
      # the β rule of the baseline's e-graph reads (a redex an added side writes),
      # so that contract_at g is a node of the graph, where these lemmas write its
      # closures, and a filling of the closure: applied to contract_at g, the
      # thunk of two holes is united with its residual thunk λy. … whose k is
      # filled (`gezi.saturation.Saturation.residualThunk`). Written inside
      # the closure's body, contract_at, function_type and candidate were fillings
